嗯，当我的丈夫李出差工作时，我对他说的最怀念的事情就是我们成年人之间的对话。

1217
00:57:44.720 --> 00:57:51.200
Because when you're with little kids, it's all little kid conversation, little kid activities.
因为当你和小孩在一起时，所有的对话和活动都是围绕着小孩的。

1218
00:57:51.500 --> 00:57:57.160
And I miss even just us saying, oh, hey, did you listen to this podcast?
我甚至怀念我们互相问候，比如，嘿，你听过这个播客吗？

1219
00:57:57.160 --> 00:57:59.440
Or did you read this thing?
或者你读过这个东西吗？

1220
00:57:59.640 --> 00:58:03.480
Or just the little adult social interaction moments.
或者仅仅是那些成年人之间的小互动时刻。

1221
00:58:03.480 --> 00:58:14.340
So I totally related to this letter because when he goes on trips, and I'm not in touch with him as much, you know, by the nature of someone traveling for work,
所以我对这封信感同身受，因为当他出差时，由于工作性质的原因，我们联系得没那么频繁，

1222
00:58:14.500 --> 00:58:19.100
that is when I will dive into just binging bitch sesh.
那时候我就会沉浸在狂听《Bitch Sesh》中。

1223
00:58:19.280 --> 00:58:24.920
Just listening to friends chitty chat about adult things, you know, or I'll listen to a bunch of best friends.
只是听朋友们闲聊成年人的话题，或者我会听很多《Best Friends》的节目。

1224
00:58:25.200 --> 00:58:29.660
I so gravitate toward these podcasts to fill that loneliness.
我非常倾向于通过这些播客来填补那种孤独感。

1225
00:58:30.120 --> 00:58:30.460
Your adult time.
属于你的成年人时光。

1226
00:58:30.620 --> 00:58:30.860
Yeah.
是的。

1227
00:58:31.440 --> 00:58:32.800
I totally get that.
我完全明白。

1228
00:58:32.800 --> 00:58:34.560
So thanks, Natalie, for your letter.
所以，谢谢你，娜塔莉，感谢你的来信。

1229
00:58:34.940 --> 00:58:39.220
Well, we had another letter from Abby from Texas and California.
嗯，我们还收到了另一封来自德克萨斯州和加利福尼亚州的艾比的来信。

1230
00:58:39.540 --> 00:58:43.180
Abby writes, not so much a question as a thank you.
艾比写的与其说是一个问题，不如说是一封感谢信。

1231
00:58:43.380 --> 00:58:47.800
My grandma who recently passed away and I would call each other lady.
我最近去世的祖母和我过去常互称对方为“女士”。

1232
00:58:48.220 --> 00:58:53.600
I don't know where it started or why, but it was always a name that only she and I would call one another.
我不知道这是从哪里开始的，也不知道为什么，但这始终是我们俩之间独有的称呼。

1233
00:58:54.060 --> 00:58:59.280
I'm reminded of her every time you guys lady one another, and I could not be more grateful.
每次听到你们互称“女士”时，我都会想起她，我对此感激不尽。

1234
00:58:59.280 --> 00:59:05.120
Thank you for the sweet reminders and thank you for staying true to what gives your friendship its own flavor.
感谢你们带来的甜蜜回忆，也感谢你们始终保持着让你们的友谊独具魅力的特质。

1235
00:59:05.580 --> 00:59:06.360
What a treasure.
真是太珍贵了。

1236
00:59:06.360 --> 00:59:09.380
Thank you again, sweet office ladies.
再次感谢你们，亲爱的《Office Ladies》。

1237
00:59:09.780 --> 00:59:10.840
I love that.
我喜欢这个。

1238
00:59:11.180 --> 00:59:13.320
Aw, Abby, lady, we love ya.
噢，艾比，女士，我们爱你。

1239
00:59:13.560 --> 00:59:14.540
We sure do, lady.
我们当然爱你，女士。

1240
00:59:14.900 --> 00:59:16.420
